-- CK-281: R-5.13.1. A type's `eq` may only read its arguments: the push
-- in it is the error `comparison_changes_value`, at the push. Red: v1 has
-- no such code and accepts the push as a write of its own parameter
-- (`accepted param`), so `check` exits 0. The code is not yet in
-- `diagnostic.Code`, so a `.codes` cannot name it (it would be malformed);
-- the `.diag` pins the code, the title (R-6.1) and the span, and its message
-- is a placeholder: the slice that adds the code blesses the real text.
pub type T
    = T (List Int)


pub eq : T, T → Bool
eq (T a) (T b) = List.length (List.push a 0) == List.length b
